      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dixon_iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s origins trace back to the mid‑19th century, founded shortly after the 1833 Black Hawk Purchase that opened Scott County to settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dixon_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1870 the Milwaukee Road railroad reached Dixon, sparking a boom that led to the creation of key local businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dixon_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The surrounding landscape features gently rolling hills, fertile alluvial soils, and expansive fields shaped by glacial and riverine forces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
